WEBVTT

00:17:59.734 --> 00:18:02.689
and half may well not be
and is more mysterious.

00:18:02.713 --> 00:18:04.595
But it's different in every case,

00:18:04.619 --> 00:18:06.774
so maybe we should just do
a health warning

00:18:06.798 --> 00:18:10.864
for the rest of the podcast and say,
"All this stuff is really complicated."

00:18:10.888 --> 00:18:13.040
There's exceptions to everything.

00:18:13.064 --> 00:18:15.136
There are no absolutes
in these categories.

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:17.840
For one thing, everyone's on a spectrum.

00:18:17.864 --> 00:18:20.198
What does that spectrum
look like, do you think?

00:18:20.222 --> 00:18:22.740
SC: You know, it depends
on which study you look at,

00:18:22.764 --> 00:18:26.076
and it's so hard because it depends
on how you're defining these terms

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:27.283
when you do the study.

00:18:27.307 --> 00:18:31.051
One that I just looked at
found 40% introvert,